Subject: [PATCH 1/3] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 4, patch 1;
 built on f9e70c167 with series 2 and 3 applied): NOTHING IN THE ENVIRONMENT
 MOVES A GATE -- THE PROJECT'S OWN VARIABLES (a further form of the planted
 case PV15, found on main's f9e70c167 while reading main's page on the
 periodic review). Series 1 closed the rule for the dates. Four other
 variables still moved a gate: with OA_REVIEW_MERGES=0 set, review-fires read
 no landings since the last review and passed, so that the block which holds
 until the review is run could be switched off by anyone; OA_POINT_REGISTER
 and OA_RETRACTIONS_LEDGER pointed point-debt and retraction-debt at another
 page; OA_HARVEST_PIN_OVERRIDE replaced a pin of harvest-debt. Each is a seam
 for a checker's own test. THE MEND: the gates' file reads the environment in
 one place, a helper that takes every variable named OA_... out of it, and
 every script a gate starts is handed that helper's environment, the two runs
 of review-due among them; the review gate takes a test's count as an
 argument. The checkers keep their seams for their own tests, which start them
 directly. ONE TEST OF MAIN'S CHANGES, with a dated note: the control of
 review-fires gave its count through the variable and now gives it as the
 argument. The lock: three tests added to
 tests/test_gates_are_a_function_of_the_commit.py: every variable named OA_...
 that the sources name is set at once, to a value that would move its reader,
 and five gates must print what they print without them; the code is read for
 a script started with the whole environment; the argument is there. On the
 commit before, all three fail, the first naming three gates whose line
 changes. Computed once; tested against planted errors, 3 of 3. 0 of 19.

